[{"result":{"data":{"json":{"id":"130","stub":{"id":"130","section":"05. Beasley Flat to Gap Creek","altname":"the Verde daily","river":"Verde","difficulty":"IIIplusstandoutIV","states":["USA-ARZ"]},"primaryGaugeStatus":{"status":"below-recommended","latestReading":{"value":"66","dateTime":"2026-05-12T03:00:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"cfs","adjustedDifficulty":null},"pointOfInterests":[{"type":"put-in","description":"Mesquite is a nice access point upstream of Beasley Flat that makes for shorter shuttle and longer float, but doesn't add any whitewater. Look for the small inconspicuous dirt lot on the left as soon as you leave private property","id":"RpJ3Fogj0bNYeeKSdCfr3","location":{"latitude":"34.473454","longitude":"-111.80085"},"name":"Mesquite RAP","distance":"-1.5","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"put-in","description":"Beasley Flat has toilets and ample parking.","id":"109677","location":{"latitude":"34.473508","longitude":"-111.801402"},"name":"Put In","distance":"0","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"rapid","description":"Off the Wall is the first named rapid and has many channels. The far right bends sharply and runs very close to the wall. The second is rocky and best at higher water. The third channel is narrow and has a nice 2ft drop in the center. The far left channel has a long flat entrance and drops steeply and blindly, often blocked by wood.","id":"9iXEC2dpUrgkF58RL9Ceo","location":{"latitude":"34.46788229","longitude":"-111.78266256"},"name":"Off the Wall","distance":"1.63","difficulty":"II+","approximate":false,"photoID":"1408TmL5l4HnOI5zOki1w"},{"type":"rapid","description":"Pre-Falls has a rocky entrance and ends in a river-wide ledge drop about 2ft high. It is pretty sticky and a good place to practice boof strokes.","id":"vV0Oh1aRHmtIjKGYD6Dug","location":{"latitude":"34.46008505","longitude":"-111.78818283"},"name":"Pre-Falls","distance":"2.4","difficulty":"III","approximate":false,"photoID":"HCKvqLfAcqOAfcVMIGFb1"},{"type":"rapid","description":"Verde Falls a 4-5ft ledge, and is runnable down to 150cfs via a narrow autoboof into a slot. At flows above 700cfs a cleaner ledge boof on the left opens up, and the right line becomes a juicy wave-hole. It has a fun rocky runout and is followed by a pretty basalt narrows that leads to a few excellent unnamed class II rapids. The falls is easily identified and portaged on river left.","id":"ICkQaIX5m8737xkJehiDS","location":{"latitude":"34.45908055","longitude":"-111.78701448"},"name":"Verde Falls","distance":"2.49","difficulty":"IV","approximate":false,"photoID":"uKbwj4HrQ2dB9aXnnHN3J"},{"type":"takeout","description":"Chasm Creek enters from the right after a long pool that features the stream gauge on the right. It is an optional hiking takeout for packrafters looking to avoid a shuttle. It is two miles up the scenic canyon to the dirt road, then 2 more miles back to the Mesquite put-in. It makes a great half lap and is a pretty hike with a section of narrows, especially nice in November with changing foliage. Be aware that this option is often part of a closed area that protects eagle nesting grounds.","id":"rLEUFaTDuHlhfuBRl2phL","location":{"latitude":"34.44637853","longitude":"-111.79076047"},"name":"Chasm Creek","distance":"3.95","photoID":"G9KG5VgnABT3ShY1tUz9Y","difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"rapid","description":"Palisades is the first named rapid on the Verde that feels \"normal\". It is wide open with few wood hazards, and is just a steep drop of small rocks. Follow the water through the shallow entrance and work your way to the left for the final plunge, which makes a surprisingly good surf wave at most water levels.","id":"ykWaMdT43dnHwtsukEeHn","location":{"latitude":"34.43898341","longitude":"-111.78325908"},"name":"Palisades","distance":"4.79","difficulty":"III","approximate":false,"photoID":"WxXFGq4L97zh8GktZC0sL"},{"type":"rapid","description":"Bull Run is probably the least notable named rapid on the Gap run, a short drop easily confused with other unnamed rapids. There is a ledge on the right is runnable if the water is deep enough, or can be avoided by moving left.","id":"9vjSlKx5ENgcQzArtkXh9","location":{"latitude":"34.43125796","longitude":"-111.77328491"},"name":"Bull Run","distance":"6.51","difficulty":"II+","approximate":false,"photoID":"vZLYzQxGQ28713CR3163l"},{"type":"rapid","description":"Punk Rock is the final named rapid before Gap Creek. Pretty much any line can be run, but at low water the easy line is right to left, finding the smoothest passage at the top and aiming to left of the boulder at the bottom.","id":"upYNSmtpOeVpMZFsbdmzO","location":{"latitude":"34.42689137","longitude":"-111.77943097"},"name":"Punk Rock","distance":"7.01","difficulty":"III","approximate":false,"photoID":"dFRFFWgqWsR4HXFoVXMpd"},{"type":"takeout","description":"The Gap Creek confluence is a large flood delta. Take out and shoulder or deflate your boat, following the creek upstream to the parking area about 1/2 of a mile. There is a fence shortly, find the gate on creek right that will help get you on the right trail.","id":"114930","location":{"latitude":"34.414189","longitude":"-111.789144"},"name":"Take Out","distance":"7.82","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false}],"alerts":[],"photos":[{"id":"879950","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"880996","description":"","caption":"Verde Falls","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":"Matt Dent","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/879950","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/879950"}},{"id":"14115","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"9309","description":"","caption":"punk rock1","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/14115","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/14115"}},{"id":"14116","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"9309","description":"","caption":"punk rock","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/14116","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/14116"}},{"id":"879951","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"880997","description":"Nice winter base flow on the Verde.","caption":"Verde above Punk Rock","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":"Matt Dent","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/879951","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/879951"}},{"id":"1970","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"4574","description":"This is the sign in the parking lot of the take-out.  This is the trailhead of the trail that you hike out of.\r\n","caption":"Take-Out Trail","poi_name":"","subject":"SIGN","author":"Jim Elson","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/1970","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/1970"}},{"id":"5328","ext":"mix","post_id":"1133","description":"First hole in the prefalls at 2200 cfs.","caption":"Prefalls on the Verde","poi_name":"Prefalls","subject":"Flagstaff Wrestling","author":"Wil Gianolla","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/5328","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/5328"}},{"id":"1969","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"4574","description":"Paul Howard, OVER 50 boating club, going over the pre falls :)","caption":"FALLS2","poi_name":"pre falls","subject":"PAUL HOWARD","author":"jim elson","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/1969","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/1969"}},{"id":"1968","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"4574","description":"This is Trevor (rear) and Bret Howard (front) catching air of the prefalls.  Half-way through the drop, Trevor then jump out of the boat!! (?)","caption":"Trevor+Bret AIRFALLS","poi_name":"Pre Falls","subject":"Bret + Trevor Howard","author":"Jim Elson","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/1968","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/1968"}},{"id":"1967","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"4574","description":"Bret dare-deviling over the pre-falls, and then resulted in a swim. \r\n\r\n\r\n","caption":"EXTREME Canoeing","poi_name":"Pre Fall","subject":"BRET HOWARD","author":"paul howard","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/1967","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/1967"}},{"id":"3483","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"5638","description":"","caption":"Hal Brooks on Verde Falls at 266 cfs","poi_name":"Verde Falls","subject":"Hal Brooks","author":"Patrick McMullen","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/3483","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/3483"}},{"id":"8976","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"6257","description":"This hole forms because of the rock directly downstream from the falls in the middle of the river.","caption":"Moenkopi 10-footer after the falls corridor","poi_name":"post-Verde Falls corridor","subject":"Moenkopi Riverworks","author":"Flagstaff HS wrestling team","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/8976","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/8976"}},{"id":"8977","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"6258","description":"Punk rock becomes a hole, find out when at moenkopi high water alert","caption":"moenkopi hysiding punk rock","poi_name":"punk rock","subject":"moenkopi high water alert","author":"","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/8977","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/8977"}},{"id":"5342","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"6259","description":"Picture perfect Hyside in a Hyside.  After the falls get buried the pour over becomes alot more grabby.","caption":"verde river prefalls in a 10 footer","poi_name":"Pre-falls","subject":"Flagstaff wrestling team tackling the prefalls","author":"Wil Gianolla","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/5342","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/5342"}},{"id":"5343","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"6259","description":"This is the first hole in the middle in the top of the prefalls.  ","caption":"Verde river pre-falls in a 14 footer","poi_name":"Prefalls","subject":"Coach","author":"Wil Gianolla","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/5343","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/5343"}},{"id":"886963","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"889695","description":"","caption":"HOT SPRINGS (River Douche Dave)  ","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":"HAWKEYE","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/886963","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/886963"}},{"id":"42626","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"10165","description":"Some how from here we ended up doing a \"McIver\", an advanced-level maneuver [as far as anyone who doesn't know-better knows...], where you go backwards through the rapids.","caption":"Verde Falls +/-1280 cfs","poi_name":"Verde Falls","subject":"Skz & Grant","author":"Zach","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/42626","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/42626"}},{"id":"886964","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"889696","description":"Got munched by Big Pink Rapid","caption":"Big Pink ","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":"","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/886964","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/886964"}},{"id":"886962","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"889694","description":"Fall Verde Trip 2010 - Mike on the bank.","caption":"Punk Rock @ 1200cfs","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":"HAWKEYE","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/886962","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/886962"}},{"id":"886965","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"889697","description":"","caption":"Big Pink (Broken Yoke)","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":"","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/886965","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/886965"}},{"id":"886966","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"889698","description":"","caption":"Big Pink (lost my shoe)","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":"","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/886966","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/886966"}},{"id":"1408TmL5l4HnOI5zOki1w","ext":"jpg","post_id":"1zDR1cDoh6SvDJVPydeTh","description":"","caption":"Off the Wall","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Landon Sawaya","poi_id":"9iXEC2dpUrgkF58RL9Ceo","photo_date":"2025-09-29T17:52:52.000Z","updated_at":"2025-09-29T17:52:52.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/1408TmL5l4HnOI5zOki1w","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/1408TmL5l4HnOI5zOki1w"}},{"id":"WxXFGq4L97zh8GktZC0sL","ext":"jpg","post_id":"0OSB16KMT61RXcKEAcK31","description":"","caption":"","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Landon Sawaya","poi_id":"ykWaMdT43dnHwtsukEeHn","photo_date":"2025-09-29T18:46:25.000Z","updated_at":"2025-09-29T18:46:25.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/WxXFGq4L97zh8GktZC0sL","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/WxXFGq4L97zh8GktZC0sL"}},{"id":"uKbwj4HrQ2dB9aXnnHN3J","ext":"jpg","post_id":"0OSB16KMT61RXcKEAcK31","description":"","caption":"","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Landon Sawaya","poi_id":"ICkQaIX5m8737xkJehiDS","photo_date":"2025-09-29T18:46:25.000Z","updated_at":"2025-09-29T18:46:25.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/uKbwj4HrQ2dB9aXnnHN3J","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/uKbwj4HrQ2dB9aXnnHN3J"}},{"id":"G9KG5VgnABT3ShY1tUz9Y","ext":"jpg","post_id":"0OSB16KMT61RXcKEAcK31","description":"","caption":"","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Landon Sawaya","poi_id":"rLEUFaTDuHlhfuBRl2phL","photo_date":"2025-09-29T18:46:25.000Z","updated_at":"2025-09-29T18:46:25.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/G9KG5VgnABT3ShY1tUz9Y","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/G9KG5VgnABT3ShY1tUz9Y"}},{"id":"HCKvqLfAcqOAfcVMIGFb1","ext":"jpg","post_id":"0OSB16KMT61RXcKEAcK31","description":"","caption":"","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Landon Sawaya","poi_id":"vV0Oh1aRHmtIjKGYD6Dug","photo_date":"2025-09-29T18:46:25.000Z","updated_at":"2025-09-29T18:46:25.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/HCKvqLfAcqOAfcVMIGFb1","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/HCKvqLfAcqOAfcVMIGFb1"}},{"id":"vZLYzQxGQ28713CR3163l","ext":"jpg","post_id":"0OSB16KMT61RXcKEAcK31","description":"","caption":"","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Landon Sawaya","poi_id":"9vjSlKx5ENgcQzArtkXh9","photo_date":"2025-09-29T18:46:25.000Z","updated_at":"2025-09-29T18:46:25.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/vZLYzQxGQ28713CR3163l","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/vZLYzQxGQ28713CR3163l"}},{"id":"dFRFFWgqWsR4HXFoVXMpd","ext":"jpg","post_id":"0OSB16KMT61RXcKEAcK31","description":"","caption":"","poi_name":null,"subject":"","author":"Landon Sawaya","poi_id":"upYNSmtpOeVpMZFsbdmzO","photo_date":"2025-09-29T18:46:25.000Z","updated_at":"2025-09-29T18:46:25.000Z","url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/dFRFFWgqWsR4HXFoVXMpd","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/dFRFFWgqWsR4HXFoVXMpd"}},{"id":"8975","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"6257","description":"10-footer approaching the falls. Notice the typewriter hole where the fish ladder usually is.","caption":"Moenkopi Riverworks high-water alert","poi_name":"Verde Falls","subject":"Moenkopi Riverworks on a mission","author":"Flagstaff HS wrestling team","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/8975","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/8975"}},{"id":"5329","ext":"mix","post_id":"6259","description":"This is the second hole and the actual falls of the prefalls.  Shortly down stream is the true falls.  As one would expect the lower the flow the steeper are both the drops and the higher the flows the shorter the drop and the more powerful  hydrolic action.  Notice the 3 man high side.","caption":"prefalls at 2200 in a 10 foot mini me","poi_name":"Prefalls","subject":"Flagstaff Wrestling team","author":"Wil Gianolla","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/5329","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/5329"}},{"id":"1965","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"4574","description":"This is Bret Howard below Verde Falls.  NOTICE: the falls in the right of the picture behind him.  Ususally at normal flows that entire ledge to the right (river left) is covered, and a boof there is the stardard move.\r\n\r\n-CODY HOWARD","caption":"Below Verde Falls","poi_name":"Below the Falls","subject":"BRET HOWARD","author":"Jim Elson","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/1965","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/1965"}},{"id":"1971","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"4574","description":"Paul and Bret Howard ELF (extremely low flow) Boating over the pre-falls.<br>\r\nCheck out the larger version of this photo by <a href=\"http://www.americanwhitewater.org/photos/?photoid=1968\">clicking here</a>.","caption":"Pre-Falls Overview","poi_name":"Pre Falls","subject":"Bret + Paul Howard","author":"Jim Elson","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/1971","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/1971"}},{"id":"1966","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"4574","description":"This is Bret Howard, AZ paddler, in a low-water descent of Verde River Falls.  This is EXTREMELY low-flows and YES he is in the kayak.  He's acually in the Riot Booster 50.\r\n","caption":"Verde Falls","poi_name":"Verde Falls","subject":"BRET HOWARD","author":"Paul Howard","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/1966","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/1966"}}],"detail":{"id":"130","permitUrl":null,"permitInfo":null,"description":"The 'Gap run' of the Verde is a river resource that Arizona is lucky to have. In this section, the river leaves its wide, populated valley behind and enters a wilderness environment with scenic canyon walls. It features roughly five class III rapids, a handful of easier ones, and a chunky IV at Verde Falls. At low to moderate water levels, this run is suitable for developing boaters who have practiced some basic boat handling and safety skills and are looking to engage with more interesting river features. There are a few surf waves and plenty of good eddies to catch. The named rapids in the first half of the run can be portaged with ease, but the second half would have a bit more bushwacking. So, don't let the IV rating deter you from venturing into this section, but be ready to recognize hazards like fallen trees and approaching rapids. Boaters commonly clear wood hazards from this run and keep the channels wide and open, making it somewhat safer than other nearby sections rated class I.\n\nIt is enjoyable down to 150cfs in small boats like packrafts and kayaks. These flows occur consistently during the cool season November-March due to groundwater springs. The water is clear and cold, so dress for the swim! In the remaining months, water is diverted for agriculture making this section borderline unrunnable unless there is a heavy snowpack (April) or extreme precipitation event (May-October).\n\nAny increase in flows from rain or snowmelt is welcome. By 300cfs the rapids become noticeably more cushioned, at 500cfs rocks begin to disappear and waves get sizeable. The channels are still open and navigable at 1000cfs and beyond, but make sure you know the lines and don't end up paddling into a dead-end forest!\n\nShuttle: The dirt road to Gap Creek is usually passable by a skilled Honda Fit driver, but it is not 'just gravel', i.e. it has some rocky sections, so it is better in a crossover at least. It makes a nice ride on a mountain bike, and could definitely be hiked by a packrafter looking to avoid dirt road driving\n\nVideo for visuals:\n\n[Packrafting the Gap run at 170cfs](https://youtu.be/_nMB5bj4x3U?si=xh8mL8NhKSqJCcl1)\n\n[Packrafting the Gap run at 700cfs](https://youtu.be/z12V0Hlsqhc?si=50tuYpkBkqfEDqd1)\n\n[Packrafting the Gap run at 1200cfs](https://youtu.be/w7QNRdtTr5k?si=YwAYK8_1K6L64eLl)\n\n[Packrafting the Gap run at 1500cfs with rapids labeled](https://youtu.be/9CHVIz8CoTw?si=fuwhzO19y7XHv0IU)\n\nAlso see the other segments:\n\n[Perkinsville to Clarkdale (classic float below Tapco RAP)](http://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/view/river-detail/127/)\n\n[Clarkdale to Camp Verde (woody, infrequently traveled class I)](http://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/view/river-detail/128/)\n\n[Camp Verde to Beasley Flats (classic class II)](http://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/view/river-detail/129/)\n\n[Childs to Horseshoe Reservoir (full wilderness section)](http://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/view/river-detail/131/)\n\n[Horseshoe Reservoir to Bartlett Reservoir](http://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/view/river-detail/132/)\n\n[Bartlett Reservoir to confluence with Salt River](http://www.americanwhitewater.org/content/River/view/river-detail/133/)","averageGradient":"0","maxGradient":"0","length":"7.9","correlations":[{"reachID":"130","isPrimary":true,"correlationDetails":{"metric":"cfs","belowRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableRangeComment":null,"mediumRunnableRangeComment":null,"highRunnableRangeComment":null,"aboveRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"highRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"beginLowRunnable":"150","beginMediumRunnable":"500","beginHighRunnable":"2000","endHighRunnable":"30000"},"gaugeInfo":{"name":"VERDE RIVER NEAR CAMP VERDE, AZ","gaugeSource":"USGS","gaugeSourceIdentifier":"09506000","gaugeFetchStatus":"ACTIVE","latestFlowReading":{"value":"66","dateTime":"2026-05-12T03:00:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"latestStageReading":{"value":"3.41","dateTime":"2026-05-12T03:00:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"location":{"latitude":"34.4483605","longitude":"-111.7898705"},"externalSourceLinks":{"sourceLink":{"url":"https://water.noaa.gov/gauges/09506000","text":"NOAA"},"secondaryLink":{"url":"https: